cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below. The
  version is the package version in pyproject.toml; cite the commit you used
  when you depend on a specific result (the daily job keeps committing data).
type: software
title: "Joint SPX/VIX Smile Calibration System"
abstract: >-
  Heston and Bates option pricing by the Lewis (2001) contour integral with a
  Black-Scholes control variate, exact VIX index and VIX futures formulas, a
  session-dated and look-ahead-gated SPX option-chain pipeline, a joint
  calibration of Heston to SPX smiles and the Cboe VIX term-structure indices,
  a delta-hedged straddle backtest priced mark-to-model (it reports a negative
  result), and the static dashboard published at https://navnoorbawa.me.
authors:
  - family-names: Bawa
    given-names: Navnoor
    affiliation: Thapar Institute of Engineering & Technology
    website: "https://navnoorbawa.me"
version: 0.22.0
date-released: 2026-10-19
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/navnoorthapar/vol-system-dashboard"
url: "https://navnoorbawa.me"
keywords:
  - stochastic volatility
  - Heston model
  - Bates model
  - VIX
  - option pricing
  - implied volatility
  - model calibration
  - backtesting
